# VERIFIED INEFFECTIVE on Cloudflare Pages - kept as documentation only.
#
# Both eyrya.com and www.eyrya.com serve the full site (both return 200). Every
# page's canonical points at www, so Google should consolidate them, but serving
# identical content on two hostnames splits inbound links and doubles the crawl
# surface. It is a hygiene issue, not the reason the site does not rank.
#
# This host-level rule was deployed and tested: eyrya.com still answered 200, so
# Cloudflare Pages does not apply `_redirects` rules that match on hostname. The
# redirect has to be created in the dashboard instead:
#
#   Cloudflare dashboard -> your domain (eyrya.com) -> Rules -> Redirect Rules
#   -> Create rule
#     When incoming requests match:  Hostname equals  eyrya.com
#     Then:  Static redirect  ->  https://www.eyrya.com  (301)
#     Preserve query string: on
#
# (or attach eyrya.com as a "Redirect" custom domain in the Pages project, which
#  Cloudflare turns into the same rule).
https://eyrya.com/*  https://www.eyrya.com/:splat  301

# Path-level rules DO work on Pages (unlike the host rule above).
#
# These five URLs belonged to content that has been deleted: two products that
# never existed (a Party LED Lights Set and an Outdoor Game Kit) and the three
# category pages that only those products populated. Without a rule they fall
# through to the 404 page; a 301 sends anyone arriving from an old link, or from
# Google's index, to the catalogue instead.
#
# Note: these paths were served with `cache-control: public, s-maxage=604800`, so
# an edge copy of the old page can outlive the deployment that removed it. Until
# that cache entry is purged (Cloudflare dashboard -> Caching -> Configuration ->
# Purge Everything) or expires, a request may still be answered from cache.
/products/party-led-lights/    /products/  301
/products/outdoor-game-kit/    /products/  301
/products/category/party-supplies/  /products/  301
/products/category/toys-play/       /products/  301
/products/category/outdoor-fun/     /products/  301
